WEBVTT

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:13.900
We've been driven to defeat?

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:15.450
Such strength!

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:19.500
That's all they've got?

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:21.250
This "Orpheus Order"?

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:28.500
Check.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.780
Locust husks, eh?

00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:58.450
Here as well, Master Rook.

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:03.200
It seems they've packed up
their Replica Ring plant.

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:04.340
Yeah...

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.060
Be careful, Kaito.

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:10.160
The Orpheus Order still seeks you.

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:27.900
Lost

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:31.020
Tesaguri de sagashiteta
I've searched, groping

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:34.940
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
The answer to a future that's been closed off

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:36.860
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
Is nowhere to be found

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:40.200
Hashiru shoudou, ima kaidoku funou
The impulse to run, it's impossible to decipher now

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.910
Found

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:46.160
Kudaketa hazu no unmei o
A fate that was supposedly smashed

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:50.630
Mijuku na yume no naka de kikoeta kitanda
I've come to hear it within that half-formed dream:

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:53.460
Saigo made I'll be there for you
Until the end, I'll be there for you

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:56.550
Tachidomaranai, kono hari dake wa
It won't stop, not this needle

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:59.890
Boku no asu o kizamu oto o tsukisasu
It will pierce the sound that engraves my tomorrow

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:01.800
Shinjitsu kara nigetara ima
If I run from the truth, then now...

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.510
Genjitsu ni mo maketara ima
If I lose to reality, then now...

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:05.850
Nani ga nokoru no?
What will remain?

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:08.060
(Nokoru no?)
(Will remain?)

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:10.440
Kazoekirenai kono kizu dake ga
These countless wounds of mine

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:13.900
Boku no kinou o zanzou to shite kataru
They tell of my yesterday as an afterimage

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.610
Unmei ga hodoketemo ima
Even if fate were unraveled, now...

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:17.440
Sonzai o kowashitemo ima
Even if my existence were smashed, now...

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:20.320
Boku no michi o yuku yo
I will travel my path

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:22.450
It's now or never

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:23.530
That is what they say

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:25.620
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:29.290
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:30.460
That is what they say

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:32.630
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:36.130
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:37.340
That is what they say

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:39.760
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:45.970
Minotaur's Lure

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:52.790
It seems so long since
we've come to school!

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:54.610
I'm still jetlagged.

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:57.610
It sure was fun, that southern island.

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:01.280
The fish were so delicious!

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:04.640
We gotta thank Erena for
taking us there, huh?

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:05.760
I guess.

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:07.750
What?!

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:10.560
You went to a southern
island with Miss Erena?!

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:13.230
Mr. Takeda, is Erena off today?!

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:16.300
Yes, the info I've received
from Mizutani is correct.

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:21.780
Morning: Film "Galactic Puzzle
Policeman, Poly Cube."

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:24.460
Afternoon: Appear on an
informative variety show.

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:28.990
Evening: Begin filming
the "Poly Cube" movie.

00:03:28.990 --> 00:03:30.120
Well done!

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:32.250
You're so informed, Mr. Takeda!

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:35.750
On her days off, Erena
is absorbed in puzzles.

00:03:35.750 --> 00:03:37.150
Therefore...

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:39.640
Will you accept once again
accept my challenge,

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:41.300
What's-Your-Name Daimon?!

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:46.090
A puzzle training camp just for men!

00:03:46.090 --> 00:03:48.600
The definition of blood
and sweat and tears!

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:50.640
This time I'll-

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:51.540
Solved it.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:55.920
What?!

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:59.320
O..Our training camp...

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:01.530
...and training tramps.

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:09.990
Einstein, Edison, Galileo,

00:04:09.990 --> 00:04:12.520
Da Vinci and Newton...

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:15.870
Peace has returned to our school,

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:18.000
and it's thanks to all of you.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.110
I haven't done anything.

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:22.820
It was the Phi-Brain children

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:25.150
who brought down the Orpheus Order.

00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:26.510
Also...

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:30.620
The fundamental problem
still hasn't been solved.

00:04:30.890 --> 00:04:34.750
Yes, the Orpheus Order
isn't exactly extinct.

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:37.920
That's just why I can't understand it.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:40.750
Your recent request...

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:45.680
Huh?!

00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:49.600
Upperclassman Jikukawa will
quit the student council?

00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:50.830
Yes...

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:53.120
And step down as the
Puzzle Club president!

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:56.100
He was so close to fulfilling
the required terms.

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:59.080
But why, Miss Vice President?

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:00.480
I don't know.

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:03.740
Whatever I ask, he laughs
and avoids the question.

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.120
Maybe his stomach hurts.

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:10.640
Look, will the school be okay?

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:12.850
If the student prez quits?

00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:14.560
It won't be okay.

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:16.400
We have to hold elections to choose

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:18.100
who will run the student council,

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:21.250
and select candidates to
be the next president ASAP.

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:25.810
The Puzzle Club has to
find a new president too.

00:05:26.730 --> 00:05:29.600
What the heck happened,
Upperclassman Jikukawa?

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:37.620
Quite a shocker, huh?

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:39.250
That the president would quit?

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:40.540
I've got it!

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:43.090
This is a message from Mr. Jikukawa!

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:43.900
Huh?

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:47.920
"Takeda, I have nothing
more to teach you."

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:53.300
"Go forth, and make your own history
with your smarts."

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:54.390
That's the gist!

00:05:54.390 --> 00:05:55.910
I..I get it!

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:57.230
My mind's made up.

00:05:57.230 --> 00:05:58.980
I'll do it!

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:01.170
So, Mr. Takeda, you'll be
president of the Puzzle Club?

00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:03.730
No...

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:09.680
Welcome home, Master Souji.

00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:12.160
I'm back, Miss Otane.

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:15.700
Where are Father and Mother?

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:19.650
The master is in Luxembourg making
a Philosopher's Puzzle.

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:24.530
The mistress is in Buenos Aires adjusting
a wind-powered puzzle.

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:27.530
They're both quite busy, aren't they?

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:33.930
Master Souji, it's a given
that once you graduate,

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:37.450
you'll join the POG as
a management trainee.

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:40.020
As a famed Giver household,

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:42.270
the Jikukawa name grows
ever more illustrious.?

00:06:42.810 --> 00:06:47.010
Now if only a young lady
would catch your fancy...

00:06:47.190 --> 00:06:49.580
Come on, that's a bit much.

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:55.270
Now then...

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:06.940
Okay, I guess we'll begin.

00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:22.720
Checkmate.

00:07:25.150 --> 00:07:28.020
But I'm not there yet...

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:30.050
At our director Rook's level.

00:07:31.190 --> 00:07:33.550
Your Opponent
Wants to Speak to You

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:39.560
My, my, you're quite skilled.

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:41.330
Well done.

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:43.560
"Excellent work, Newton," I should say.

00:07:45.370 --> 00:07:49.460
Still trying to recruit people, Minotaur?

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:51.980
Rather, Mr. Orpheus Order?

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:54.880
I have reappeared to recruit you,

00:07:54.880 --> 00:07:56.830
would perhaps be more accurate.

00:07:57.430 --> 00:08:00.680
That last move was a splendid attack.

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:02.430
In an instant, you leapt straight

00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:04.960
to the answer without
a moment's hesitation.

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:09.570
It is the Givers who create puzzles

00:08:09.570 --> 00:08:11.900
and the Solvers who then release them.

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:14.490
The way you solve puzzles links
both of these points of view.

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:15.470
Huh?

00:08:17.450 --> 00:08:19.840
The data I received, that
you had previously sought

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:22.020
to be a Solver, was correct.

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:28.270
That is why I once
reappeared to recruit you.

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:33.260
When Giver and Solver are both assembled
in one Phi-Brain,

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:35.220
the Puzzle of God may be challenged.

00:08:36.010 --> 00:08:38.780
That was the POG's theory, yes?

00:08:38.970 --> 00:08:42.140
I'm not sure. Was it?

00:08:42.140 --> 00:08:45.690
The Phi-Brain is the ultimate human,

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:49.520
one with the skills of
both Giver and Solver.

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:51.920
That is the definition
of a true Phi-Brain.

00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:58.800
Hence, the Orpheus Order seeks
those with both abilities.

00:08:59.530 --> 00:09:03.120
Doubt quickly sought to recruit Gammon,

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:05.580
but that was because he sensed Gammon

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:07.440
was like-minded, nothing more.

00:09:09.290 --> 00:09:10.690
However...

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:13.590
You, it was you,

00:09:13.590 --> 00:09:16.220
the one suited to be a Phi-Brain.

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:19.470
You are the one suited to wear a Ring.

00:09:21.010 --> 00:09:23.010
A Replica Ring?

00:09:23.770 --> 00:09:25.080
It's just a fake, right?

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:29.060
Whether it's fake is not important.

00:09:29.060 --> 00:09:33.650
What is important is if you can
become a true Phi-Brain.

00:09:33.650 --> 00:09:35.050
Am I wrong?

00:09:35.530 --> 00:09:38.030
I'm grateful for your invitation,

00:09:38.030 --> 00:09:39.800
but I've given up on that.

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:42.810
Is that truly so?

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:47.590
Young Master, it's not
good to stay up too late.

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:49.310
Okay.

00:09:51.170 --> 00:09:52.850
I'll be in touch again.

00:09:54.590 --> 00:09:56.820
Was that a phone call from a friend?

00:09:57.800 --> 00:10:00.990
No, talking to myself.

00:10:13.730 --> 00:10:15.870
Good morning, Miss Vice President!

00:10:16.190 --> 00:10:19.530
Ah, Itou, Daimon.

00:10:19.530 --> 00:10:20.530
'Sup?

00:10:20.530 --> 00:10:24.160
Oh! What's with those
bags under your eyes?

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:27.140
I couldn't sleep at all last night.

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:30.360
I...

00:10:31.210 --> 00:10:32.620
I've always thought the

00:10:32.620 --> 00:10:35.950
student council president
would be president.

00:10:36.760 --> 00:10:40.860
I wanted to work with him
till the end of his term.

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:44.660
I knew in the end I'd be sad,
and I thought I was ready for that.

00:10:44.930 --> 00:10:48.290
But he quit so suddenly...

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:51.140
What are you two whisperin' about?

00:10:51.140 --> 00:10:52.980
Shut up, you man!

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:56.180
So, you ain't gonna be
the student council president?

00:10:57.650 --> 00:10:59.740
I think you're the only one who could

00:10:59.740 --> 00:11:02.010
follow Upperclassman Jikukawa.

00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:04.120
M..Me?

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:07.740
Impossible, I could never follow
Upperclassman Jikukawa.

00:11:08.330 --> 00:11:11.020
All of you commuting to school!

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:16.500
Candidate
Student Council President
Naoki Takeda

00:11:11.210 --> 00:11:16.530
Vote for Naoki Takeda for your next
student council president!

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:18.630
They're already campaigning?!
Naoki Takeda!

00:11:18.630 --> 00:11:20.300
Why is he running?
Cast your vote for Naoki Takeda.

00:11:20.300 --> 00:11:22.910
'Cuz fools rush in.
Cast your vote for Naoki Takeda.

00:11:22.930 --> 00:11:34.190
Candidate
Student Council President
Naoki Takeda

00:11:23.090 --> 00:11:26.720
This is what our president said this:

00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:28.310
"I'm sure Takeda"

00:11:28.310 --> 00:11:30.670
"could blow a wind of genius over this

00:11:30.670 --> 00:11:32.880
school far in excess of mine."

00:11:33.370 --> 00:11:34.210
See?!

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:38.370
Yes, I am the one acknowledged
by the student council

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:41.060
president as his successor!

00:11:41.060 --> 00:11:45.200
Rather, a genius better called the
Second Souji Jikukawa!

00:11:44.820 --> 00:11:53.290
Candidate
Student Council President
Naoki Takeda

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:48.280
Please, make Naoki Takeda your next
student council president!

00:11:48.280 --> 00:11:50.490
Cast your vote for Naoki Takeda,

00:11:50.490 --> 00:11:53.310
the next (unofficial) president
of the Puzzle Club!

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:58.810
Th..The Second Souji Jikukawa, he says?!

00:11:59.460 --> 00:12:00.380
M..Miss Vice President?

00:12:01.510 --> 00:12:04.130
Upperclassman Jikukawa's
student council...

00:12:04.130 --> 00:12:08.330
I won't allow it to be used by the
rabble for personal gain!

00:12:09.760 --> 00:12:10.630
I've made up my mind.

00:12:11.260 --> 00:12:14.100
I will run for student
council president too!

00:12:14.310 --> 00:12:19.070
Tamaki
Chieno

00:12:14.890 --> 00:12:19.090
Sound puzzles lie in
a sound academic life.

00:12:19.440 --> 00:12:22.400
I will uphold Jikukawa's system,

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:25.590
seeking to create an
academic lifestyle of order

00:12:24.690 --> 00:12:26.550
Here you go!

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:27.210
and free thinking.

00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:33.080
For your next student council president,
elect Hachiro Okudera!

00:12:33.080 --> 00:12:36.440
Okudera, if you please!

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:38.830
At Root Gakuen, I have
held positions on both

00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:40.440
the Broadcast and Library Committees,

00:12:40.460 --> 00:12:53.180
Hachiro
Okudera

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:43.160
and my older brother is a genius puzzler

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:44.800
who achieved a remarkable 8th place

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:49.050
in the Asian preliminaries
of the Puzzle World Cup!

00:12:49.050 --> 00:12:53.210
I'm the thoroughbred of the
puzzle world, Hachiro Okudera!

00:12:53.520 --> 00:12:56.440
Everyone, everyone, please cast
your vote

00:12:56.440 --> 00:12:59.300
for Hachiro Okudera!

00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:03.170
Those who vote right now

00:13:03.170 --> 00:13:07.700
will receive special compensation
from me as council president!

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:10.120
Any club that casts an
organized vote for me

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:13.520
will receive various accommodations

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:15.130
in the form of their club budget.

00:13:15.660 --> 00:13:16.960
Best of luck to you!

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:18.500
Thank you very much.

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:19.540
Good luck.

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:21.850
Thank you, I'll do my best.

00:13:22.670 --> 00:13:26.670
It's turned into a ruckus 'cuz of
Upperclassman Jikukawa.

00:13:27.630 --> 00:13:30.870
Upperclassman Jikukawa
has his own reasons.

00:13:31.430 --> 00:13:34.640
Then, he should've talked to us.

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:35.620
We're pals, right?

00:13:35.810 --> 00:13:37.140
Well...

00:13:38.640 --> 00:13:40.880
Happy-smiley, freeze-o!

00:13:41.230 --> 00:13:42.440
Ana...

00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:45.370
It's like he's bright, but he's cold.

00:13:46.190 --> 00:13:47.840
Souji doesn't look well.

00:13:48.200 --> 00:13:53.390
Yeah, Upperclassman Jikukawa is
surely happy-smiley, freeze-o.

00:13:53.530 --> 00:13:55.410
I get it...

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:56.890
That makes no damn sense!

00:13:57.250 --> 00:14:02.480
Cast your vote for Naoki Takeda!

00:14:02.750 --> 00:14:05.820
My, my, quite the handful, aren't they?

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:08.570
It's your fault, ain't it?

00:14:09.380 --> 00:14:10.210
Kaito!

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:13.140
Why'd you quit all of a sudden?

00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:14.080
Sir.

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:17.330
Maybe I'll go on a trip.

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:19.630
That's what I thought, at least.

00:14:20.020 --> 00:14:20.710
Huh?

00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:24.770
You turned down the Orpheus Order's Ring,

00:14:24.770 --> 00:14:26.630
and becoming a Phi-Brain too.

00:14:27.170 --> 00:14:32.950
Section Phi looks like it's
on the verge of shutting down.

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:37.890
This is unusual, for a meddler like you.

00:14:39.160 --> 00:14:42.400
And what do you know about me?

00:14:44.170 --> 00:14:48.090
Being president never suited me.

00:14:48.090 --> 00:14:52.830
I really am a selfish,
self-serving individual.

00:14:53.090 --> 00:14:56.390
But this is a load off my shoulders.

00:14:56.390 --> 00:14:59.140
With you here, the student
council will be all right

00:14:59.140 --> 00:15:02.790
and Chieno will make the
council work somehow.

00:15:02.940 --> 00:15:04.770
The Puzzle Club...

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:06.300
I kind of worry about that though.

00:15:07.750 --> 00:15:09.300
You sayin' this for real?

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:10.300
Of course.

00:15:14.410 --> 00:15:15.660
Well, fine.

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:18.450
I'm sure you've got your own plans,

00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:20.310
things you wanna do.

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:23.250
You're goin' on a trip, right?

00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:24.960
I'll be waitin' for a souvenir.

00:15:25.840 --> 00:15:26.940
Kaito!

00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:43.080
An invitation?

00:15:43.480 --> 00:15:47.340
Oh, jeez, I can't believe
he knows this number too.

00:15:50.570 --> 00:15:51.760
That location is...

00:15:52.030 --> 00:15:54.010
Aah, I don't have enough fliers!

00:15:56.620 --> 00:15:58.830
No other copy machines?

00:16:01.990 --> 00:16:04.550
Huh? Upperclassman Jikukawa?

00:16:14.260 --> 00:16:16.870
I wonder where Upperclassman
Jikukawa's going?

00:16:24.890 --> 00:16:26.560
That thing is Tamaki?

00:16:26.560 --> 00:16:27.690
Yes!

00:16:27.690 --> 00:16:29.170
It don't look human.

00:16:33.030 --> 00:16:34.030
Nonoha?

00:16:35.990 --> 00:16:37.220
Upperclassman Jikukawa?!

00:16:59.550 --> 00:17:02.680
Waiting in the Chamber of the Armlet?

00:17:02.680 --> 00:17:06.520
I never thought I'd come here again...

00:17:10.980 --> 00:17:13.070
Upperclassman Jikukawa went
to the mountains in the rear?

00:17:13.070 --> 00:17:15.530
Yeah, Nonoha tried following,

00:17:15.530 --> 00:17:16.640
but she lost sight of him.

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:20.760
Apparently, he looked like something
was bugging him.

00:17:22.120 --> 00:17:23.020
It can't be!

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:29.940
The mountains in the rear?

00:17:33.350 --> 00:17:34.500
Over there...

00:17:36.070 --> 00:17:37.570
That pulley puzzle...

00:17:38.220 --> 00:17:39.230
Minotaur...

00:17:40.260 --> 00:17:41.280
Also...

00:17:43.050 --> 00:17:44.930
an Armlet of Orpheus.

00:17:45.810 --> 00:17:46.870
Found him!

00:17:47.600 --> 00:17:49.080
Look at this!

00:17:54.570 --> 00:17:56.360
Upperclassman Jikukawa!

00:17:56.360 --> 00:17:57.550
Why is he there?!

00:18:01.570 --> 00:18:03.180
Welcome, Newton.

00:18:12.210 --> 00:18:13.150
This is...

00:18:15.700 --> 00:18:18.950
Yes, a puzzle you know well.

00:18:19.590 --> 00:18:23.180
The rules are a little different
from last time though.

00:18:23.180 --> 00:18:25.140
If you pull the wrong rope,

00:18:25.140 --> 00:18:28.460
an explosion will go off and
this cavern will collapse.

00:18:29.020 --> 00:18:33.270
Root Gauken will also sink to the
depths of Hell, no doubt.

00:18:34.730 --> 00:18:37.720
I see, that's quite bad.

00:18:38.190 --> 00:18:39.990
However, I'm at a loss.

00:18:39.990 --> 00:18:41.610
I'm a Giver.

00:18:41.610 --> 00:18:44.220
Solving puzzles isn't my strong point.

00:18:44.530 --> 00:18:45.770
In that case...

00:18:47.580 --> 00:18:49.230
You should use this.

00:18:55.590 --> 00:18:57.090
Yo, the hell is that?

00:18:57.090 --> 00:18:58.460
A Replica Ring!

00:18:58.460 --> 00:18:59.990
What's goin' on?!

00:19:03.510 --> 00:19:05.830
Tell them, Cube.

00:19:08.850 --> 00:19:11.100
Hey, man, you know something?

00:19:11.100 --> 00:19:12.380
Spit it out, dude!

00:19:13.400 --> 00:19:17.380
Upperclassman Jikukawa
told me to keep quiet.

00:19:18.070 --> 00:19:20.360
The Orpheus Order contacted you?

00:19:20.360 --> 00:19:21.170
Yeah...

00:19:21.860 --> 00:19:24.130
It looks like I've been
chosen as their next

00:19:24.130 --> 00:19:25.970
guinea pig for the Replica Rings.

00:19:27.120 --> 00:19:29.280
Still, this is my chance.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:33.520
If all goes well, we could get some
information about their Rings.

00:19:33.870 --> 00:19:36.960
The Rings' weaknesses,
how to remove them...

00:19:36.960 --> 00:19:40.320
I said if I knew that, I'd put one on.

00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:46.090
Because that's the one
thing I can do right now.

00:19:46.090 --> 00:19:47.450
But it's too dangerous!

00:19:47.680 --> 00:19:50.420
There's no way one of their fakes
could swallow me up.

00:19:50.890 --> 00:19:53.520
If anything, I will control it.

00:19:55.440 --> 00:19:56.880
Upperclassman Jikukawa...

00:19:57.150 --> 00:20:00.940
Of course, I have no clear
idea of what will happen.

00:20:00.940 --> 00:20:04.640
I'll have to expect the worst.

00:20:05.070 --> 00:20:07.170
And be ready for it, of course.

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:11.750
So, Upperclassman Jikukawa quit
the student council because...

00:20:11.750 --> 00:20:12.540
Yes.

00:20:13.960 --> 00:20:15.280
That selfish bugger!

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:16.880
Kaito!

00:20:16.880 --> 00:20:17.960
Kaito!

00:20:17.960 --> 00:20:18.980
Damn!

00:20:25.260 --> 00:20:26.930
What's the matter?

00:20:26.930 --> 00:20:29.340
If you don't solve this soon,
the academy will be in danger.

00:20:32.350 --> 00:20:35.020
Don't fear, just put the Ring on.

00:20:35.020 --> 00:20:37.310
Do that and you'll be a Phi-Brain,

00:20:37.310 --> 00:20:39.340
able to save the school!

00:20:40.150 --> 00:20:42.590
Those words don't count for much.

00:20:43.490 --> 00:20:45.090
A Phi-Brain, huh?

00:20:48.530 --> 00:20:50.010
When Kaito bonded with the Armlet

00:20:50.010 --> 00:20:52.380
that refused me,
becoming a Phi-Brain,

00:20:53.160 --> 00:20:55.580
my mind was made up:

00:20:57.500 --> 00:21:00.280
I would give my dream to him.

00:21:00.840 --> 00:21:02.490
I wouldn't interfere.

00:21:09.600 --> 00:21:12.430
That idiot, doin' something
so dangerous on his own!

00:21:13.260 --> 00:21:15.710
Never suited you, my ass!

00:21:17.730 --> 00:21:18.840
Sure enough,

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:22.010
you're the student council president,
Souji Jikukawa!

00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:27.510
Oh, my, out of options, huh?

00:21:27.910 --> 00:21:32.030
Do I die along with the school
or do I put this Armlet on?

00:21:32.030 --> 00:21:33.770
One or the other?

00:21:34.330 --> 00:21:36.270
It seems the time has come.

00:21:43.340 --> 00:21:44.360
Kaito!

00:21:48.220 --> 00:21:49.760
Where's Upperclassman Jikukawa?

00:21:49.760 --> 00:21:50.780
Right here.

00:21:55.100 --> 00:21:56.730
Upperclassman Jikukawa!

00:21:57.770 --> 00:22:00.040
The school is all right now.

00:22:00.520 --> 00:22:02.190
And the Replica Ring?

00:22:02.190 --> 00:22:04.400
Yes, no problem.

00:22:05.190 --> 00:22:06.220
So...

00:22:06.650 --> 00:22:09.220
Please fight with me, Kaito.

00:22:19.350 --> 00:22:23.610
The Replica Ring has been grafted
onto Souji Jikukawa.

00:22:38.710 --> 00:22:40.050
Eiyuukidori
Playing the hero

00:22:40.050 --> 00:22:44.940
Itsudatte shinjita muteki no kankaku
A sense of invincibility you always believed in

00:22:45.550 --> 00:22:51.370
Tatakatte iru no wa chikyuu no tame nanka ja nai
You're not fighting for the sake of the world or anything

00:22:51.370 --> 00:22:54.160
Motto maipeesu de
It's for a more leisurely

00:22:54.160 --> 00:22:59.230
Sou, motto shoujiki na onegai no tame
Yeah, more straightforward request

00:22:59.600 --> 00:23:07.670
Nandotonaku kizutsuitemo tachiagare, hero
Even if you're wounded over and over, rise up, hero

00:23:07.670 --> 00:23:13.220
Kitto daijoubu, kimi o mamorunda
It's sure to be all right, I'll protect you

00:23:13.610 --> 00:23:17.040
Machigai da to shitemo tomarenai
Even if it's wrong, it can't be stopped

00:23:17.040 --> 00:23:20.650
Seikai ka nante wakaranai
I don't know if it's the right answer

00:23:21.550 --> 00:23:24.660
Donna toki demo original ni
No matter the situation

00:23:24.660 --> 00:23:27.400
Step o fumidashiteku
I'll take those first steps, originally

00:23:27.400 --> 00:23:30.770
Dramatic ni, mawaru sekai de
On this spinning world, I'm searching, dramatically

00:23:30.770 --> 00:23:34.430
Kiwameita wonder sagashiteru
For wonders that sparkle

00:23:35.190 --> 00:23:38.430
Boku, shijou saikou no tabi o tsuzukeyou
Me, I'll keep going on the greatest journey in history

00:23:38.430 --> 00:23:42.740
Image shite shiawase na mirai e
To the happy future I imagined

00:23:44.430 --> 00:23:46.060
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:51.380
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:51.380 --> 00:23:52.800
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:54.710 --> 00:23:56.260
(Mirai e)
(To the future)

00:24:02.440 --> 00:24:04.620
I never dreamed that one day I could

00:24:04.620 --> 00:24:06.550
puzzle challenge you, one on one.

00:24:06.810 --> 00:24:08.480
Oh, this Ring?

00:24:08.480 --> 00:24:11.530
Not to worry, I haven't changed at all.

00:24:11.530 --> 00:24:14.360
More importantly,
I've prepared the best game of all.

00:24:14.360 --> 00:24:16.070
Of course, you'll do it, right?

00:24:16.070 --> 00:24:17.600
My graduate thesis?

00:24:18.240 --> 00:24:20.090
Next time, "Forbidden Fruit"

00:24:20.660 --> 00:24:23.210
Come, let puzzle time begin...

00:24:21.660 --> 00:24:26.670
Forbidden Fruit

00:24:23.210 --> 00:24:25.290
Einstein, Kaito Daimon!
